                <pb facs="0131" n="19" sameAs="frus:frus1907p1/pg19"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 4478/3.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Wilson to the Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Buenos
                                Aires</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1907-10-05"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">October 5,
                    1907</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Wilson states that the situation in the Province of Corrientes is serious,
                    but confined to that Province, and that several fights have taken place between
                    the revolutionary and government forces. Informs Mr. Root that <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Las Palmas</hi>, a steamer belonging to an American
                    citizen, has been seized by the revolutionists and that he has requested the
                    Government to take the necessary measures for its return. Says that the
                    revolutionists have taken two boats belonging to Italian subjects.)</p>
            </div>
